Package: ggdmc
Type: Package
Title: Hierarchical Bayesian Inference for Cognitive Models
Version: 0.2.9.0
Date: 2025-09-18
Authors@R: c(person(given = "Yi-Shin", family = "Lin", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "yishinlin001@gmail.com"))
Maintainer: Yi-Shin Lin <yishinlin001@gmail.com>
Description: Tools for fitting hierarchical Bayesian cognitive models using Differential Evolution Markov chain Monte Carlo (DE-MCMC). Designed for cognitive scientists and psychologists, it supports models including the Linear Ballistic Accumulation (LBA), Diffusion Decision Model (DDM) and Cognitive Diagnostic Model (CDM). The package implements parallel C++ routines for large-scale applications, providing parameter sampling, simulation, model building, posterior recovery, and convergence diagnostics. Methods build on prior work including Turner et al. (2013) <doi:10.1037/a0032222>, ter Braak (2006) <doi:10.1007/s11222-006-8769-1>, and Hu & Tsui (2010) <doi:10.1016/j.csda.2008.10.025>, and the parameter-mapping framework of Heathcote et al. (2018) <doi:10.3758/s13428-018-1067-y>.
